::Q1::What is AI pair programming?
{ 
~An automated replacement for all software teams
=Using an AI tool to assist a developer while they write and work with code
~Two human developers sharing one keyboard
~A method for training an operating system
}

::Q2::Which practice can help Copilot provide more useful suggestions? 
{
~Removing all context from the file
~Using vague names everywhere
~Accepting every suggestion immediately
=Writing clear comments and function signatures
}

::Q3::What should a developer do before accepting a Copilot suggestion? 
{
=Evaluate whether it is correct and appropriate for the task
~Assume it is correct because it was generated by AI
~Delete all tests
~Run it automatically in production
}

::Q4::What is a limitation of AI pair programming tools? 
{
=Suggestions can be incorrect, insecure, or unsuitable for the specific codebase
~They can only generate comments
~They never produce syntactically valid code
~They always understand business requirements perfectly
}

::Q5::What is a sound approach to a Copilot suggestion that looks plausible? 
{
=Inspect, test, and verify it before relying on it
~Assume testing is unnecessary
~Trust it solely because it looks plausible
~Use it in production immediately
}